{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/4/codegen_prompts/1.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/4`\n- 题号：`1`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/4/1.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"1\">\n- `description`：根据每个矩形框内的标记像素朝向，确定该框应与哪个方向上的同色锚点配对，然后用锚点颜色填充框的内部。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干个由 Grey 像素构成的一像素厚空心矩形框。\n  - 每个框的某一条边上有恰好一个非 Grey、非 Black 的彩色标记像素（如 Red、Blue、Green），嵌在边框像素中，替换了该位置的 Grey 像素。\n  - 网格中另有若干个 2x2 的彩色实心锚点方块散布在框外，锚点颜色与某些框的标记颜色相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每个矩形框，确定其标记像素所在的边（上、下、左、右），该边指向框外的方向即为\"朝向\"。\n  - 沿朝向方向寻找第一个与标记同色的 2x2 锚点方块。\n  - 将该矩形框内部（不含边框）的所有背景像素填充为锚点的颜色。\n  - 保持框的 Grey 边框、标记像素、锚点方块不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：标记像素所在的边既编码了搜索方向，又通过颜色指定了配对锚点；解题者需要同时归纳方向编码和颜色配对两层规则。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/8a6d367c, eval/13e47133, eval/332f06d7, eval/dbff022c, train/1478ab18, train/5b37cb25, eval/581f7754, eval/0934a4d8\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2840\nmechanism=0.3421\nlexical=0.0166\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:square, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8a6d367c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"upper colored template mask s\",\n  \"dst\": \"rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"13e47133\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2709\nmechanism=0.3351\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:frame, object:marker, object:rectangle, operation:flood_fill, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/13e47133.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/13e47133.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.\n- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.\n\nRule:\n- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.\n- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.\n- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.\n\nKey insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Isolated colored pixels in each region expand by drawing alternating concentric rectangular frames parallel to region boundaries until the entire region is filled.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"isolated single colored pixels within each partitioned region s\",\n  \"dst\": null,\n  \"match_cond\": \"\",\n  \"path\": \"draw rectangular frame parallel to region boundary, then shrink inward by 1 pixel and repeat alternating s.color with background until region is filled\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"paint s.color on current frame, alternate with region background color on next frame, continue inward\",\n  \"transform\": \"\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"concentric frames\",\n    \"region partitioning\",\n    \"alternating pattern\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2561\nmechanism=0.2932\nlexical=0.0263\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:marker, object:square, operation:flood_fill\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2472\nmechanism=0.2531\nlexical=0.0152\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:frame, operation:flood_fill, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1478ab18\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2242\nmechanism=0.2883\nlexical=0.0206\ncode_feature=0.2000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:marker, object:square, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/1478ab18.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/1478ab18.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nPaint the teal outline of the right triangle determined by the missing corner of the grey-marker square.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is an orange background with exactly four foreground marker pixels of one color. The markers have a square bounding box: three markers are bbox corners, and the fourth marker is inside that square.\nRule\nFind the one corner of the marker bounding square that has no marker. That missing corner is the right-angle vertex of a right isosceles triangle; paint its two axis-aligned legs and the opposite diagonal in teal, leaving existing marker pixels unchanged.\nKey insight\nThe present corner marker opposite the missing corner is a decoy; the three triangle vertices are the missing corner and the two marker corners adjacent to it.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"four grey marker pixels whose bbox is a square with exactly one missing corner\",\n  \"transform\": \"paint teal on the outline of the right triangle inside the square: the missing bbox corner is the right-angle vertex, the two adjacent marker corners are the other vertices; keep grey markers unchanged\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
